A||||3||Jhonny||Will 3.8 liter Pontiac Bonneville injectors fit the Fiero ?||||5||
Z||000000||Jhonny||01-04-2001||04:28 AM||||Hi all,<P>Is it possible to use 3.8 L Bonneville injectors as replacement for the Fiero<BR>injectors ?<BR>I dont't know if the Bonneville injectors has a higher flowrate and if this presents a problem ....<P>/// Jhonny<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR><A HREF="http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html" TARGET=_blank> Welcome to Vadstena</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||01-04-2001||07:42 AM||||I believe they are physically the same size, but the flowrate would be far too great for a stock motor.  Even 3.4 injectors on a 3.1 make it run poorly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jhonny||01-04-2001||02:10 PM||||Does injectors from other GM cars fit ?<BR>Corsica, Beretta etc ?<BR>Used Fiero injectors are in short supply on this side of the pond and new ones are expensive.<P>Thanks<P>Jhonny<P>------------------<BR>Jhonny Sokura<BR>Vadstena, Östergötland Sweden<BR><A HREF="http://www.vadstena.se/turism/engelsk/index.html" TARGET=_blank> Welcome to Vadstena</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||HF6582||01-04-2001||02:59 PM||||Ford mustang injectors 19# will work, but flow may be to much on a stock motor.<P>Scott||||reg||1
